(FIL-63: of the four invalid Seek targets probed here, the three the
 manual actually names - a line past EOF, a position < 1, an invalid
 descriptor - all set the error flag. A byte past EOF does not, and the
 manual does not claim it should: LANGUAGE.md names only "line past EOF",
 and lseek(2) is explicitly allowed to seek past the end. That absence is
 the compiler being POSIX-correct on a case the manual is silent about, not
 a finding.
 **Refreshed 2026-08-21.** Until vox #47 (0.4.8) the line-past-EOF handler
 did not fire either - see Discrepancy 3, now resolved - so this probe
 recorded only two of the three. The missing line "a line past EOF set the
 error flag" is present now.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-63.vox -o p && ./p
 actual output:
   a position below 1 set the error flag
   a line past EOF set the error flag
   an invalid descriptor set the error flag
   survived every invalid seek
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
open a file for writing called seedfile at "vf_scratch/files/lines.txt".
Write "alpha\nbeta\ngamma\n" to seedfile.
Close seedfile.
open a file for reading called source at "vf_scratch/files/lines.txt".
Seek source to byte 0.
On error print "a position below 1 set the error flag".
Seek source to line 99.
On error print "a line past EOF set the error flag".
Seek source to byte 9999.
On error print "a byte past EOF set the error flag".
Close source.
open a file for reading called bogus at 2147483647.
Seek bogus to byte 4.
On error print "an invalid descriptor set the error flag".
print "survived every invalid seek".
